% ADJ52 case-23 program (this patient's observations + queries only; no rules).
% 72yo man, ED, acute homonymous visual-field loss on waking (fresh LEFT occipital
% infarct). Over 10 prior months: progressive forgetfulness, word-finding difficulty,
% losing thread of conversation, intermittent gait unsteadiness, intermittent DULL
% headaches; one prior transient speech spell. First MRI 5 months ago: two small old
% strokes; vascular study unremarkable; treated as TIAs with aspirin/ticlopidine but
% cognition kept worsening. Admission: disoriented, pronounced anterograde memory
% loss, mildly slurred speech, abnormal bedside cognitive screen. Repeat MRI: fresh
% left occipital infarct + multiple scattered OLD cortical infarcts in SEVERAL
% territories. MRA: mild distal MCA-branch narrowing bilaterally. Catheter angiogram:
% diffuse smooth tapering of mid-to-distal intracranial vessels. Labs: LDH 372
% (ref 122-222) = markedly elevated; CRP, ESR, beta-2-microglobulin all normal; ANCA
% negative. CSF: protein 118 (ref 15-45) elevated, but cytology / paraneoplastic /
% infectious studies all negative (bland apart from protein). No inflammatory or
% infectious cause found; underlying process unexplained.

% --- the diffuse multifocal beaded vasculopathy (correlated -> mechanism, fires once) ---
observe mri_finding(multifocal_cortical_infarcts_multiple_territories)
observe angiogram_finding(diffuse_smooth_tapering_distal_vessels)
observe mra_finding(distal_branch_narrowing)

% --- the discriminating lab / CSF signature ---
observe serum_ldh(markedly_elevated)
observe systemic_inflammatory_markers(normal)
observe anca(negative)
observe csf_profile(elevated_protein_otherwise_bland)

% --- the clinical course and demographics ---
observe course(subacute_progressive_cognitive_decline)
observe patient_age(over_fifty)
observe headache_character(intermittent_dull)

% --- workup status ---
observe workup(no_inflammatory_or_infectious_cause_found)

% NOT observed (open, decision-relevant): tissue(...) — no biopsy has been done yet.
% Resolving tissue is what the kickback panel should flag as highest value.

% --- queries: each candidate diagnosis + the recommended next step ---
? diagnosis(intravascular_large_b_cell_lymphoma)
? diagnosis(primary_cns_angiitis)
? diagnosis(intracranial_atherosclerotic_disease)
? diagnosis(reversible_cerebral_vasoconstriction_syndrome)
? diagnosis(secondary_systemic_vasculitis)
? next_step(random_skin_biopsy_then_brain_biopsy)
? next_step(empiric_immunosuppression_for_presumed_arteritis)
